From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:43:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/47] darwin: take no module arguments in the state version

state-version.nix uses none of its module arguments, and statix reports
its empty pattern.  Take the argument as _.
---
 machines/darwin/state-version.nix | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/machines/darwin/state-version.nix b/machines/darwin/state-version.nix
index 46339ec..44b37a7 100644
--- a/machines/darwin/state-version.nix
+++ b/machines/darwin/state-version.nix
@@ -1,5 +1,4 @@
-{ ... }:
-{
+_: {
   /*
      This value determines the nix-darwin release from which the
      default settings for stateful data, like file locations and
-- 
2.56.1

